'''Uxiu''' ({{IPA|an|uːʃjuː|label=pronounced "Oo-shee-oo"|small=no|lang=an}}; {{Langx|kp|Uksiwu}}) is the administrative seat of [[Bayara]], and the ninth-most populous city in [[Balisca]]. 

The Uxiu region was inhabited by the [[Oka (indigenous peoples)|Oka]] and [[Itáwára people|Itáwára]] indigenous peoples until the arrival of the ''[[W:Bandeirante|bandeirante]]'' [[Ambròs Huesca de Almazán]] in 1638. In the late 1780s, the modern settlement of Uxiu was established upriver from the port of [[Macaio]] as a staging point for the exploration of the interior and the exploitation of local resources. In 1883, Uxiu became the western termini of the [[Trans-Atlántido Railroad]] with the completion of the [[Ansilta Tunnel]], connecting it with [[Guadalajara]] in [[Hesperia]]. Most of the [[Immigration to Balisca|immigrants]] who came to Bayara in the 19th century to settle the [[Western Plains (Balisca)|Western Plains]] passed through Uxiu. 

